    <item>
      <title>How to change any entries in the database in SE16 or SE11</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/se16-se11-change/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 25 Dec 2021 14:51:25 +0100</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/se16-se11-change/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Sometimes we are forced to change some database entries. There are many reasons like a new s-note from SAP or incorrect values in the technical table. Every SAP table can be changed via SE16 or SE11 transaction - all you need to have is a &lt;mark&gt; debug with change role&lt;/mark&gt; assigned to your user. In this article you can find youtube video, and bellow is detailed step by step instruction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Video tutorial&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div style=&#34;text-align:center;&#34;&gt;
&lt;iframe width=&#34;560&#34; height=&#34;315&#34; src=&#34;https://www.youtube.com/embed/evxRzGTY5lE&#34; title=&#34;YouTube video player&#34; frameborder=&#34;0&#34; allow=&#34;accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture&#34; allowfullscreen&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Step by step instruction how to change entry in SE16&lt;/h2&gt;
1. We have to login into the system and go to the SE16 or SE11 transaction. Put the table name, and display the required result. When you see the record which you want to edit, please select it and put  **/hs** in the transaction textbox.
&lt;figure class=&#34;align-center &#34;&gt;
    &lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/se16_se11_change/1.png#center&#34;
         alt=&#34;se11 window&#34; width=&#34;80%&#34;/&gt; 
&lt;/figure&gt;

&lt;ol start=&#34;2&#34;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Click on the Display icon in the upper panel. Normally you should see a detailed view, but now the debugger will run instead. This step will not work if you do not have the debug authorization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;figure class=&#34;align-center &#34;&gt;
    &lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/se16_se11_change/1a.png#center&#34;
         alt=&#34;se11 table&#34; width=&#34;80%&#34;/&gt; 
&lt;/figure&gt;

&lt;ol start=&#34;3&#34;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the debugger window, please click on &lt;strong&gt;Breakpoints-&amp;gt; Breakpoint at-&amp;gt; Breakpoint at Subroutine&lt;/strong&gt;. New window should open.
&lt;figure class=&#34;align-center &#34;&gt;
    &lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/se16_se11_change/2.png#center&#34;
         alt=&#34;Breakpoint window&#34; width=&#34;80%&#34;/&gt; 
&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
